For an adult with a disability, you can apply for Supplemental Security Income (SSI) online if you meet certain requirements [p261].

You are eligible to file online for SSI if:
- You are between the ages of 18 and 65;
- You have never been married;
- You aren't blind;
- You are a U.S. citizen residing in one of the fifty states, District of Columbia, or the Northern Mariana Islands;
- You haven't applied for or received SSI benefits in the past; and
- You are applying for Social Security Disability Insurance at the same time as your SSI claim.

If you don't meet these requirements, you may still need to apply in person at a Social Security office.
